    "summary": "I built a seed-starting tray with four cells side by side in a compact 2×2 cluster on one level. Each cell holds a half-depth drained bin (hex-bin-half-drain). I capped the open outside faces with solid end caps and bolted the joints together. To show what the tray is for, I filled each bin with soil and planted a seedling. The soil and seedlings are display props only and aren't in the parts list. The configurator's check found no rule issues, and its collision check came back clear. In all it's 22 parts: 4 bases, 4 bins, 14 caps and 5 joint bolts. Print estimate: about 1,777 g of filament and roughly 2,594 minutes (about 43 hours).",
